n assume a student who failed every math class might struggle in engineering. You can assume someone who faints at the sight of blood might not love surgery. Those are directly relevant, highly predictive, and based on their individual record. What you can’t do—or at least shouldn’t—is assume a whole personality profile and career destiny from a single demographic category. That’s not the death of common sense; it’s just the wisdom to know when common sense needs a double-check from the individual it’s about.
